    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0804" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to the Chief of Staff</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eisenhower</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-06-06">6 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>823. It was suggested by me to Doctor T. V. Soong that the Chinese Government
                    might wish to notify the Chinese Supply Commission in Washington of its approval
                    for purchase of Chinese manned Liberty <pb facs="0805" n="795" xml:id="pg795"/>
                    ships reference 89251.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d493-f1"/> Doctor Soong informs me
                    that Minister Yu Ta-wei<anchor n="60" xml:id="d493-f2"/> will give immediate
                    approval to formal application for purchase.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d493-f1" n="59" xml:id="d493-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram of May 24, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d493-f2" n="60" xml:id="d493-f2-content">
                <p>Chinese Minister of Communications.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
